content.text:
Pretty small. The simplest fix would be one of:

**Option A: Remove the aggressive fallback** (~3 lines)
```go
// Delete lines 217-221:
// if len(currentSessions) == 0 {
//     currentSessions = sessions
// }
```
If no sessions match current HEAD, just don't add a checkpoint trailer. Simple.

**Option B: Add recency check** (~5 lines)
```go
// Only reuse from sessions active in last 30 minutes
if session.LastCheckpointID != "" && 
   time.Since(session.StartedAt) < 30*time.Minute &&
   (len(session.FilesTouched) == 0 || hasOverlappingFiles(...)) {
```

**Option C: Check ancestry instead of exact match** (~10 lines)
```go
// Instead of BaseCommit == HEAD, check if BaseCommit is ancestor of HEAD
if isAncestor(repo, session.BaseCommit, currentHeadHash) {
    currentSessions = append(currentSessions, session)
}
```

Option A is the smallest and safest - if we can't confidently match a session, don't add a potentially wrong trailer. The downside is losing the "split commits" feature where you can spread Claude's work across multiple manual commits.

Want me to do Option A now? It's a 3-line deletion.

