The old code (lines 217-220 before fix):

```go
// If no sessions match current HEAD, fall back to all sessions
// (for backward compatibility with sessions created before BaseCommit tracking)
if len(currentSessions) == 0 {
    currentSessions = sessions  // ← FALLBACK TO ALL SESSIONS
}
```

That fallback meant: "if no sessions match HEAD, search ALL sessions" — which allowed old sessions with stale `lastCheckpointId` to be picked up.

The fix changes it to `return nil` (skip trailer) instead of falling back.

